      "writtenOn": "2026-08-08T02:09:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason is I tested with asan and the build is broken.  asan changes the addressing and doesnt work with offsets in the current form.\n\nThe reason i used single \"m\" with offset is x86 32 bit generates an instruction sequence to find the address (call/pop) that uses another register, and multiple \"m\" often cause out of registers error.  Or a performance issue.\nAnother solution is pass a single \"r\" address, which commits to using a register, even for 64 bit.\nA more elegant way is create a helper function that takes the constants as a parameter, which is a pointer, and optionally put it in a struction.\n\nI\u0027ll remove the asan fix from this change.",
      "parentUuid": "3ba5d882_258513c2",
